status:
  scope: >-
    The unconditional comparator targets are A (Delta^35 to R^6) and B for
    d >= 36. The literal Challenge audit preserves all seven interface
    definitions and both theorem types. Their actual proof bodies and
    dependencies were accepted by Lean checker, NanoDa and con-ron with
    exit code 0. Geometric blocking by 5*d markers is proved for d >= 18.
    The new concrete comparison, its chosen target section, and the full
    fifteen-color relative induction have each passed Lean. The d > 17
    conclusion is conditional on the explicit proposition
    AkopyanResearch.ConcreteComparison.RequiredRelativeLifting, whose
    proof is not provided. The final working project gate passed at
    2026-11-24T06:11:59Z, as recorded in verification/final-delivery/REPORT.md:
    132 source modules, 131 proof-module owners and 6144 declarations
    (4611 public, 1533 private; 4625 theorems and 1432 definitions),
    including guards for 59 selected theorems and 16 selected definitions.
    All 23 tests passed and all 145 recorded verification inputs were
    unchanged. The build emitted 349 warnings; the fresh audit emitted none.
    Four selected
    Completion theorem proofs, including the conditional d > 17 theorem,
    also passed all three independent checking components. A separate
    compiled-interface comparison matched all nine types and seven
    definition bodies between independently imported Challenge and Solution.
    The latest modules prove exact pair ranks, PairState coverage and orbit
    classification, the full homeomorphism of the concrete target with a
    standard path-space homotopy fiber, the continuous linear normal model
    of actual paired tests, and a strong deformation retraction of their
    local complement Q onto the exact balanced locus K. Connectivity of
    the comparison remains unproved. These modules are included in the
    successful integrated working gate. The final source-release gate passed
    at 2026-11-24T06:13:11Z with the same 145 input hashes; see
    verification/clean-delivery/REPORT.md. It cumulatively cold-built 120
    modules, then eleven additions, then PairCollapsedLocus. Entry modules
    were rebuilt; the final stage preserved all 129 other object hashes.
    No project build objects were copied from the working tree. This is
    a 120+11+1 source rebuild, not repeated from-zero builds of all 132 modules.
    Seven selected model declarations (two theorems and five definitions)
    and 38429 dependency declarations were accepted by all three checking
    components at 2026-11-24T06:09:39Z; see verification/model-kernels/REPORT.md.
    That certificate belongs to the 131-module snapshot. The subsequently
    added PairCollapsedLocus module proves a strong deformation of the
    actual closed chart complement D onto its equal-common-component
    subtype. It passed both final full Lean owner/build gates but was not
    included in that export. A final source preflight checked all 147 regular
    Lean files, including fifteen diagnostics, for module headers, the
    10000-line limit and admissions outside Challenge; maximum length was
    9336 lines, with no errors. The
    official sandboxed Comparator returned exit 1 during bubblewrap tmpfs
    setup with ENOENT; it has not accepted the project in this environment.
  # Lexical proof-source scan excludes the independent Challenge and
  # verification/tests directories, exactly as scripts/check_structure.py.
  # Evidence: draft-proof-token-count.json (131 proof modules, hashed).
  sorry_count: 0
  sorry_in_definitions: 0
  axioms: ["propext", "Classical.choice", "Quot.sound"]
  main_results:
    - declaration: "AkopyanSixfold.tverberg_counterexample"
      file: "Solution.lean"
      sorry_count: 0
      axioms: ["propext", "Classical.choice", "Quot.sound"]
